{% doc %}
  The opening cover: the arrow alone, then ONLY, then the full lockup, then
  it clears to whatever the page is — the hero's video, on the home page.

  Rendered from the layout rather than a section so it covers every page and
  paints before anything else has a chance to. It is the same wordmark
  throughout, with more of its letters showing at each step, so the arrow —
  the Y — holds the centre while the words grow around it.
{% enddoc %}

{% liquid
  assign duration = settings.preloader_duration | default: 2000
  assign step = duration | divided_by: 3
%}

<site-preloader
  class="preloader"
  style="
    --preloader-background: {{ settings.preloader_background | default: '#0F80BE' }};
    --preloader-color: {{ settings.preloader_color | default: '#FFFFFF' }};
    --preloader-duration: {{ duration }}ms;
    --preloader-step: {{ step }}ms;
    --preloader-limit: {{ duration | plus: 4000 }}ms;
  "
  role="presentation"
  aria-hidden="true"
>
  {%- comment -%}
    The wordmark whole, not cut apart. Its letters are already separate paths,
    so the script can show them a group at a time, and the slide that keeps
    the arrow centred is applied to the <svg> itself — which sidesteps the
    clip the artwork carries, since a translate inside it would run letters
    straight into the edge of that clip.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <span class="preloader__mark">
    <span
      class="preloader__art"
      ref="stage"
    >
      {% render 'logo-wordmark' %}
    </span>
  </span>
</site-preloader>

<script
  src="{{ 'preloader.js' | asset_url }}"
  type="module"
></script>

{% stylesheet %}
  /*
   * Covers everything, including the header and the fixed logo — for the
   * couple of seconds it is up, it *is* the page. It leaves by fading, so
   * whatever is behind is already in place underneath rather than arriving
   * after it.
   */
  .preloader {
    position: fixed;
    inset: 0;
    z-index: 2000;

    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;

    background-color: var(--preloader-background, #0f80be);
    color: var(--preloader-color, #ffffff);

    /*
     * The fallback, and the reason this is an animation rather than a
     * transition: if the script never runs — it fails, it is blocked, the
     * element is never upgraded — this still ends. A preloader that cannot
     * leave is worse than no preloader at all.
     */
    animation: preloader-give-up 0.5s ease var(--preloader-limit, 6000ms) forwards;
  }

  .preloader[data-done] {
    opacity: 0;
    visibility: hidden;
    pointer-events: none;
    transition: opacity 0.5s ease, visibility 0s linear 0.5s;

    /* Done is done: the fallback must not fade it back in. */
    animation: none;
  }

  @keyframes preloader-give-up {
    to {
      opacity: 0;
      visibility: hidden;
    }
  }

  /* Wide, because the first state is one glyph out of twenty-one: at any
     size where the finished lockup looks modest, the arrow alone is a speck.
     The letters never change size — the mark is drawn once, this is the size
     it is drawn at — so this is the only lever on how legible the opening
     frame is.

     Shared with the hero's opening logo (--ocp-logo-lockup-width), so the
     handover from cover to hero is the same mark at the same size. */
  .preloader__mark {
    display: block;
    width: var(--ocp-logo-lockup-width);
  }

  /* The slide that keeps the arrow centred as the words appear either side.
     Written as a share of its own width, so it holds at any rendered size —
     the shift is measured in the drawing's units, and the drawing is exactly
     this element wide. */
  .preloader__art {
    display: block;
    transition: transform 0.55s cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
  }

  .preloader__art svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
  }

  .preloader__art path {
    fill: currentcolor;
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.45s ease;
  }

  /*
   * The escape hatch, if the script never upgrades the element: show the
   * lockup rather than sit on an empty blue field.
   *
   * It has to be on a *delay*. `:not(:defined)` is true on every load, not
   * only the broken one — a `type="module"` script is deferred by definition,
   * so a rule that reveals the letters outright reveals ONLY COFFEE PROJECT
   * for the whole wait, and the sequence then starts by taking letters away.
   * The delay is the preloader's own duration: a script that has not run by
   * the time the cover would have finished is not going to run.
   */
  site-preloader:not(:defined) .preloader__art path {
    animation: preloader-fallback-letters 0.4s ease var(--preloader-duration, 2000ms) forwards;
  }

  @keyframes preloader-fallback-letters {
    to {
      opacity: 1;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .preloader__art {
      transition: none;
    }
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
    .preloader__art path {
      transition: none;
    }
  }
{% endstylesheet %}
